      "content": "hey so i was doing that internship at the lab last summer (the one with the heavy particle beam testing) and ever since that one shift where the containment seal flickered... i've been seeing these weird colored distortions in my peripheral vision. like, right before something big happens, there's this heavy red haze or these sharp blue streaks. it's not like a visual impairment though, it feels more like i'm seeing the atmosphere change. is there any theoretical physics concept that would explain seeing something like pattern-based probability densities? like maybe some kind of high-energy particle interaction with the optic nerve?",
